@startuml
!include theme.iuml
allowmixing
title Compiler runtime classes and function modules
hide empty members
' @class compiler.lexer.tokenizer.Token
class Token <<namedtuple>> {
  text: str
  category: str
  _asdict() {generated}
}
' @class compiler.parser.grammar.GrammarError
class GrammarError
class ValueError <<external>>
' @class compiler.parser.analysis._Transformations
class _Transformations {
  steps: list[dict]
  expansions: int
  snapshot_units: int
  append(alternatives, rhs)
  record(operation, before, after, description)
}
rectangle "tokenizer.py / learned.py <<modules>>\ntokenize(), classify_token(), analyze_sentence()\nbuild_lexicon(entries)" as Lexer
rectangle "grammar.py <<module>>\nread_grammar(), snapshot()\nGrammar = dict[str, list[list[str]]]" as Grammar
rectangle "analysis.py <<module>>\ntransform_grammar(), calculate_first()\ncalculate_follow(), build_table()\nleft_recursive_nonterminals()" as Analysis
rectangle "service.py / predictive.py <<modules>>\nanalyze_grammar(), parse_tokens()\nparse_analysis()" as Parser
Lexer ..> Token : constructs one per raw token
GrammarError --|> ValueError
Grammar ..> GrammarError : rejects invalid notation
Analysis ..> _Transformations : creates one per transformation run
_Transformations ..> GrammarError : rejects work / size overrun
Analysis ..> Grammar : snapshots / aliases
Parser ..> Analysis : calls
Parser ..> Grammar : reads / validates
note bottom of _Transformations
  A real private production class: included.
  Its operation log is a list of dictionaries,
  not a collection of invented Step objects.
end note
legend bottom
  Token is an application-defined runtime class generated by namedtuple.
  Grammar, Production, analysis results and parse traces are aliases/dictionaries.
  There is no LexerService, Grammar class, Parser class or compiler database.
  Lifetimes of function-local values are not drawn as class compositions.
endlegend
@enduml
